# Fixing Discovery Loop Execution

This plan outlines the steps to "force" the inactive nodes in the discovery loop to execute, allowing us to debug the flow and see their logs. Based on the analysis of [recursive_flow.py](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py) and [logic_gate.py](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/models/logic_gate.py), the inactive nodes are likely being bypassed due to early `exit` decisions by the [LogicGate](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/models/logic_gate.py#65-257) or by the V5.1 Circuit Breaker.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This plan involves temporarily altering core threshold values to intentionally force the state machine into an infinite loop (or up to the `max_loop_count`). This is strictly for debugging purposes to trigger the nodes ([targeted_slm_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1470-1509), [interpolation_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1550-1571), etc.) and trace their logs. We will revert these changes after identifying the root cause.

## Proposed Changes

### Configuration Modifications
We will modify the core thresholds of the [LogicGate](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/models/logic_gate.py#65-257) to ensure that it never immediately passes (exits) on the first loop iteration, forcing the system into the slower discovery loop path.

#### [MODIFY] logic_gate.py (file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/models/logic_gate.py)
- Modify the [__init__](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/models/lnn_knowledge_base.py#67-101) method defaults:
  - Change `high_confidence_threshold` from `0.85` to `1.01` (preventing early PASS).
  - Change `low_confidence_threshold` from `0.4` to `0.0` (preventing early FAIL/Noise exit).

---

### Node Execution Tracing
To ensure we capture exactly when a node starts executing, we will add un-ignorable error-level logs at the very top of each node function.

#### [MODIFY] recursive_flow.py (file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py)
- **Add Tracing Logs**: Inject `logger.error("[DEBUG EXECUTION] <Node Name> is running")` at the top of:
  - [vjepa_brain_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#305-393)
  - [latent_director_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#398-710)
  - [fusion_engine_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1297-1393)
  - [logic_gate_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1395-1468)
  - [targeted_slm_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1470-1509)
  - [interpolation_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1550-1571)
- **Bypass Circuit Breaker**: Inside the [logic_gate_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1395-1468) function in [recursive_flow.py](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py) (around line 1424), temporarily comment out the `if (gate_decision.anomaly_type.value == "volumetric" and not perception.is_volumetric_data_fresh):` block. Currently, this block returns `"continue_perception"`, which bypasses the [targeted_slm_node](file:///d:/Antigravity/Test%20VJEPA%20EVENTBASED%20LLM/Implementation/v2_logic/controllers/recursive_flow.py#1470-1509). We want to disable this for the test.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Once these modifications are applied, we will run your V5.1 testing script (or main pipeline) that initializes the system.
2. We will monitor the `Log error.txt` or console output.
3. We expect to see the sequence of `[DEBUG EXECUTION]` logs, proving that the nodes are now actively participating in the graph sequence.
4. After reviewing the logs to understand *why* the loops were terminating prematurely under normal conditions, we will **revert** these temporary changes and apply the final fix.
